# Implement the complete serialized package transaction loop

Implement and execute the complete serialized package transaction loop for
every operation family.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Implement and execute the complete serialized package transaction loop for
  every operation family.

## Dependencies

Parent task: `apply-conversion-plans-through-tested-native-unreal-mcp-commands`.

## Evidence

The repository-local MCP client and project-side Python contracts are healthy:
all 267 editor-control tests pass with the canonical pytest configuration, and
the project Python guards pass before native launch.

A live UE 5.8.1 smoke on 2026-08-17 reached the native project boundary. The
editor binary itself starts, but `shar.uproject` cannot load because its SHAR
modules do not yet have Linux editor binaries for this source-engine build.
A project target build demonstrated the cause rather than an MCP transport
failure: UnrealBuildTool planned the missing native modules and their enabled
plugin dependencies before the endpoint could start.

The live build was stopped when its shared action graph began writing
`libUnrealEditor-*` products into the external Engine installation. That is
outside this repository's session boundary. `-NoEngineChanges` is insufficient
for this constraint because UE 5.8.1 explicitly permits creation of new Engine
files while blocking modification of existing ones. The required MCP Engine
plugins (`ToolsetRegistry`, `ModelContextProtocol`, and
`ModelContextProtocolServer`) also have no prebuilt Linux binaries in that
installation, so a repository-only session cannot complete the live endpoint
without an Engine installation prepared with those plugin binaries or a future
build layout that keeps every output below this repository.

The transaction loop therefore remains open. Fake-server and schema/plan tests
are not being treated as a substitute for the blocked native MCP smoke.
